some of the most iconic characters in  star wars history have been of  mandalorian ancestry but one of the  biggest questions people seem to have is  who's the best mandalorian denjarian or  boba fett welcome back everyone i'm  rocket riley and since they now both  have their own series on disney plus i'm  here to help answer the question of who  is the better man delorean between boba  fett and denjarin the first thing we'll  be comparing the two on is their armor  best car armor is one of the most  important symbols of mandalorian culture  typically featuring an easily  recognizable mandalorian helmet this  armor is made from best car a rare metal  which is able to withstand blaster bolts  and even lightsabers the question though  is who has the better armor denjarin or  boba fett  then jaren had his original armor  destroyed after an intense battle with a  mudhorn and received new best car armor  as their award for bounty this shiny new  armor sets den apart from the rest of  the bounty hunters and has a very high  level of structural integrity boba fett  however has some of the most iconic  mandalorian armor of all time ever since  his appearance in the empire strikes  back fans have admired his unique green  armor featuring a distinctive dent in  the helmet this armor was even able to  protect boba from the acid in the  sarlacc stomach since boba's armor has a  more unique look and a long history  going all the way back to its original  owner and boba's father jango fett boba  fett beats out denjarin on who has the  best armor while denjarn likely has more  protective armor boafetz simply has a  better story and is more recognizable as  a star wars icon the next item to  discuss is the two mandalorians  hand-to-hand combat abilities  mandalorians are typically trained from  a young age in melee combat and these  two are no different boba fett was  raised by legendary bounty hunter jango  fett and dinjarin was raised as a  foundling by the children of the watch  both of which helped form them into  formidable fighters we've seen much of  denjaran's capabilities in hand-to-hand  combat but he relies heavily upon his  weapons and gadgets boba fett however  has shown his melee strength on multiple  occasions although he was easily knocked  into the sarlacc pit by a blind man boba  fett is one of the most impressive  fighters in the star wars galaxy likely  due to his training with the tuscans  because of this training he's able to  take down large groups of enemies with  melee attacks only it's this training  with the tuscans i believe which puts  boba in the lead for this category the  next category to compare the two on is  their weapon abilities both din jarn and  boba fett have a large arsenal of  weapons on them at all times including a  series of blades blasters grappling  cords and wrist flame throwers weapons  unique to boba fett include a backpack  rocket and knee pad rocket darts weapons  unique to denjarin include the whistling  birds and the ambient phase pulse rifle  while both feature their own unique  weaponry din jarns are better simply due  to the fact that they're able to take  down many specific individuals in a  group and also completely disintegrate  his enemies these weapons and his skill  in using them puts dinjarn in the lead  for this category the next item to  discuss is the two mandalorian sidekicks  for this category we'll be pitting din  jaren's child figure grogu against boba  fett's partner fenik shand din jarn  rescued grogu in the first season of the  mandalorian and this child has become  one of the most beloved star wars  characters of all time fenik shand on  the other hand was rescued by boba fett  in the first season of the mandalorian  as well but she has yet to become a star  wars icon like grogu while fenik shand  has strong combat abilities grogu's  likability and force sensitivity put him  and din jarn in the lead for this  category the next category we'll be  discussing is each character's power  symbol boafet's symbol of power is his  place as daimyo of mos espa on the  throne of the late job of the hut this  throne however has been somewhat  discredited by the other hutts as well  as by the pikes who have begun  controlling more of tatooine's  territories denjarin's symbol of power  is the darksaber which he won in combat  from maf gideon the darksaber is the  symbol of leadership for the entirety of  the mandalorian people and it was built  by tar vizla the first person to be both  mandalorian and a jedi this darkseber is  one of the coolest symbols of power in  the star wars galaxy one of the most  recognizable lightsabers of all time  it's for these reasons that denjarin  wins in this category now let's discuss  the two individuals character arcs boba  fett has been somewhat inconsistent in  his character development we saw him as  a child on the prequels and in the clone  wars series as well as shortly in the  original trilogy he didn't seem to  develop much from his original character  until his time in the sarlacc pit and  then with the tuscans but then he seemed  to completely change as a character with  little screen time to see that character  growth he changed from a merciless  bounty hunter to a forgiving and  welcoming leader seemingly on a dime  then jaren on the other hand has had  plenty of time to show his growth at the  beginning of the first season of the  mandalorian we saw a ruthless bounty  hunter who adhered strictly to the way  of the mandalore by the end of the  second season however den had become a  somewhat open-minded father figure to  the child grogu it's for this reason  that dinjaran most certainly has a  better character arc than boba fett for  the next section i'd like to compare  instances for each character when they  were at their most resourceful for  denjarin i'd argue that the time he was  most resourceful was when he took down  moff gideon's tie fighter using his  jetpack and wrist grappling cord din  flies over the tie fighter grapples the  wing of the ship and places a bomb on  the wing for boba fett i believe the  time he was most resourceful was when he  escaped from the sarlacc pit boba uses  the oxygen from a nearby stormtrooper to  give himself some air to breathe then  uses that oxygen as fuel for his wrist  flamethrower which he uses to escape i'd  argue that in this case bobo was more  resourceful relying not just on his own  gadgets but also using his surroundings  to his advantage  for the final category let's compare the  two characters motivations  in the book of boba fett series it isn't  quite clear what boba fett's motivations  are we know his goal is to lead from  jabba's palace with respect rather than  with fear but we haven't truly been  given a reason as to why he wants to do  this denjaran on the other hand has a  very strong motivation in his series his  goal is to protect the child grogu and  return him to his own kind the jedi he  has a strong motivation to protect grogu  because he sees him basically as his own  son and he would put protecting grogo  above all else including his own life  it's for this reason that denjarin has a  stronger character motivation than boba  fett that brings the final score to boba  fett with three and din jarn with five  so i'd argue that din jaren is  ultimately the best mandalorian and he's  become one of the most iconic star wars  characters ever in a very short amount  of time for a complete rundown of  everything we know so far about another  iconic star wars character series check  out this video on the upcoming obi-wan  kenobi series also don't forget to  subscribe like this video and thanks for  watching rocky riley
 

